# Prototype-Based Open Set Recognition

A PyTorch implementation of a **Prototype-Based Open Set Recognition (OSR)** system.

The system uses a trained ResNet50 to convert images into feature vectors and then determines whether a test image belongs to one of the known classes or should be rejected as **UNKNOWN**.

---

## How It Works

The system works in two main stages:

### 1. Learning the Known Classes

First, ResNet50 is trained normally on the known classes.

For example:

```text
Known Classes:
    Cat
    Dog
    Horse
```

After training, the final classification layer is removed and ResNet50 is used as a **feature extractor**.

Each image is converted into a 2048-dimensional feature vector:

```text
Image
  ↓
ResNet50
  ↓
2048-dimensional feature vector
```

These feature vectors represent the images in a feature space.

---

## 2. Creating Class Prototypes

For every known class, all of its training feature vectors are collected and averaged.

For example:

```text
Cat images
   ↓
Feature vectors
   ↓
Mean
   ↓
Cat Prototype
```

The same process is performed for every known class.

If there are three known classes:

```text
Cat    → Prototype 0 → [2048 values]
Dog    → Prototype 1 → [2048 values]
Horse  → Prototype 2 → [2048 values]
```

Each prototype represents the **centroid of its class in the feature space**.

---

## 3. Measuring Distance

When a new image is given to the system, ResNet converts it into a 2048-dimensional feature vector.

The system then calculates its distance from **every known-class prototype**.

For example:

```text
                    Distance
Test Image → Cat      0.21
Test Image → Dog      0.83
Test Image → Horse    1.12
```

The smallest distance identifies the class whose prototype is closest to the test image.

In this example:

```text
Closest prototype → Cat
```

---

## 4. Determining Whether the Image Is Actually Known

Simply finding the closest class is not enough.

An unknown image will also be closest to *some* known class, even if it does not actually belong to that class.

Therefore, the system also uses a **distance threshold**.

The threshold is obtained from the distance distribution of known training samples.

The system calculates the distance of every training image to its closest known-class prototype and uses the **95th percentile** of these distances as the current rejection threshold.

Conceptually:

```text
Known training images
        ↓
Distance to closest prototype
        ↓
Distance distribution
        ↓
95th percentile
        ↓
OSR Threshold
```

---

## 5. Open Set Decision

At test time, the system performs two decisions:

### Step 1 — Find the closest known class

```text
Test Image
    ↓
Feature Vector
    ↓
Distance to all prototypes
    ↓
Minimum distance
    ↓
Closest known class
```

### Step 2 — Check whether the distance is acceptable

```text
Minimum distance
       ↓
Compare with threshold
       ↓
 ┌───────────────┐
 │               │
 ≤ threshold   > threshold
 │               │
 ↓               ↓
Known Class    UNKNOWN
```

Therefore, even if an unknown image is technically closest to a known class, it will be rejected if it is too far away from that class prototype.

---

## Complete Working Pipeline

```text
                 TRAINING
                    │
                    ▼
             Known Images
                    │
                    ▼
                ResNet50
                    │
                    ▼
          2048-D Feature Vectors
                    │
                    ▼
        Group Features by Class
                    │
                    ▼
         Calculate Class Mean
                    │
                    ▼
              Prototypes
                    │
                    ▼
       Calculate Training Distances
                    │
                    ▼
      Minimum Distance per Image
                    │
                    ▼
          95th Percentile
                    │
                    ▼
             OSR Threshold


                 TESTING
                    │
                    ▼
               Test Image
                    │
                    ▼
                ResNet50
                    │
                    ▼
          2048-D Feature Vector
                    │
                    ▼
       Distance to Every Prototype
                    │
                    ▼
            Minimum Distance
                    │
                    ▼
          Closest Known Class
                    │
                    ▼
        Compare with Threshold
                    │
             ┌──────┴──────┐
             ▼             ▼
       Within threshold   Too far
             │             │
             ▼             ▼
       Known Class       UNKNOWN
```

