## Example

Suppose the system knows:

```text
Cat
Dog
Horse
```

An unknown **Elephant** image is passed to the model.

Its distances might be:

```text
Cat      → 0.82
Dog      → 0.91
Horse    → 0.76
```

The closest class is technically:

```text
Horse → 0.76
```

But suppose:

```text
OSR Threshold = 0.40
```

Since:

```text
0.76 > 0.40
```

the system rejects the prediction:

```text
Prediction → UNKNOWN
```

This prevents the model from being forced to classify every image as one of the known classes.

---

## Core Idea

The system does not simply ask:

> "Which known class is this?"

It asks two questions:

```text
1. Which known class is it closest to?

2. Is it close enough to that class to be considered known?
```

This gives the system the ability to recognize samples that fall outside the known classes.

